---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Callout from "@dst/ui/Callout.astro";
---
<Layout
  title="Local Directory"
  description="Cafes, markets, fitness, and restaurants in and around Azizi Riviera, organized for residents rather than visitors comparing developments."
>
  <section class="container hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">Local directory</p>
    <h1>What's actually walkable</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Organized the way a resident thinks about it — what's downstairs, what's
      a five-minute walk, and what needs a car — rather than a flat list.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="container">
    <h2>On the promenade</h2>
    <p>
      The ground-floor retail strip is the main day-to-day resource: a mix of
      cafes, casual dining, a supermarket, and convenience retail spread
      across the buildings that front the canal walkway. Coverage isn't
      uniform yet — newer buildings have thinner retail than the
      longer-established stretch — so what's actually open changes as the
      development fills in. Treat any specific business list as a snapshot,
      not a fixture.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="container">
    <h2>Fitness</h2>
    <p>
      Most buildings include a residents' gym as part of the building
      amenities, which covers day-to-day training for most people. For
      anything more specific — classes, pools, personal training — the
      nearby Meydan One and Downtown areas are a short drive and carry more
      dedicated fitness options than the promenade itself does today.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="container">
    <h2>Groceries and markets</h2>
    <p>
      A supermarket on the promenade covers routine shopping without leaving
      the development. For a wider selection — specialty and international
      groceries in particular — residents typically drive to the larger
      supermarkets in Meydan or Business Bay rather than relying on the
      on-site option for everything.
    </p>
  </section>

  <Callout kind="warn">
    This page describes categories of what's available, not a fixed roster of
    named businesses — the promenade's tenant mix changes as the development
    continues to fill in. If you're relying on a specific business being
    open, confirm it directly rather than from this page alone.
  </Callout>
</Layout>

<style>
  .hero { padding-top: var(--space-5); }
  .lede { font-size: var(--step-1); color: var(--ink-muted); max-width: 65ch; }
</style>
